```
iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 → ACCEPT (narrow exception only)
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto tcp → DROP
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto udp → DROP
iifname "eth2" → DROP   ← 28 packets dropped (ICMP, everything)
```

**Every packet transiting from the rest of the network (arriving on eth2) is dropped.** Router6 itself reaches PC16 fine (it originates traffic locally on eth1), but any forwarded packet from router3 via eth2 hits the catch-all DROP. Return traffic (PC15→PC11) also dies here: PC11's reply travels router4→router3→router6 eth2, then hits the DROP rule.

PC11 also checks out fine: gateway `192.168.200.1` (router4 eth0), directly connected — no issue there.

